  "title": "Nansen's Fram expedition",
  "summary": "In June 1893 the Norwegian ship Fram left Kristiania for the Arctic and was frozen into the ice north of Siberia to drift for nearly three years. Nansen and Hjalmar Johansen left the ship in 1895 and reached 86°14′ N, then wintered on Franz Josef Land; the ship and the men returned to Norway in 1896.",
